---
// src/pages/library.astro
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Pazhassi Raja Smaraka Granthalayam | Mananthavady, Wayanad">
  <article
    class="w-full border-b border-zinc-900 py-16 sm:py-24 px-6 sm:px-12 selection:bg-[#D9381E] selection:text-[#F6F4EE]"
  >
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-12 sm:space-y-16">
      <!-- Page Header -->
      <header class="space-y-4 border-b border-zinc-300 pb-8">
        <div
          class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-500 flex items-center gap-2"
        >
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#D9381E] transition-colors"
            >&larr; Home</a
          >
          <span>/</span>
          <span>Institutions</span>
        </div>

        <h1
          class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight text-[#161616] leading-none"
        >
          Pazhassi Raja Smaraka Granthalayam
        </h1>

        <p
          class="font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#D9381E] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider"
        >
          Mananthavady &bull; Wayanad, Kerala
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Narrative Text -->
      <div
        class="space-y-8 font-serif text-lg sm:text-xl text-zinc-800 leading-relaxed sm:leading-loose"
      >
        <p
          class="first-letter:text-6xl first-letter:font-black first-letter:float-left first-letter:mr-4 first-letter:leading-none first-letter:text-[#161616]"
        >
          Across Kerala, rural and municipal libraries have long stood at the
          core of social progress. When P.N. Panicker and fellow visionaries
          organized the library movement in the mid-twentieth century, they
          envisioned libraries not as silent warehouses for books, but as
          vibrant, democratic village halls where citizens could gather, educate
          themselves, read daily newspapers, and engage in civic debate.
        </p>

        <p>
          The <strong>Pazhassi Raja Smaraka Granthalayam</strong> in Mananthavady
          was born out of this grassroots movement. Established in memory of Kerala
          Varma Pazhassi Raja, the historic ruler of the Kottayam dynasty who fought
          against British East India Company forces across the rugged terrain of Wayanad,
          the library stands as a living cultural institution rooted in the heritage
          of the region.
        </p>

        <p>
          Affiliated with the Kerala State Library Council, the granthalayam has
          steadily built a rich and varied collection over decades. Its shelves
          house everything from foundational Malayalam literature, poetry, and
          social essays to contemporary fiction, translated world classics,
          historical works, children’s literature, and reference volumes.
          Alongside its lending collection, the library maintains an active
          reading room where daily newspapers and weekly periodicals are
          available to all.
        </p>

        <p>
          Beyond lending books, the library has continually functioned as an
          open cultural center in Mananthavady. Over the years, it has hosted
          literary gatherings, reading circles, book discussions, commemorative
          programs, student competitions, and educational seminars. It provides
          an accessible, non-commercial public space where people of all
          generations—school students, teachers, local workers, retired elders,
          and independent scholars—can learn and converse freely.
        </p>

        <p>
          In a rapidly changing media landscape, Pazhassi Raja Smaraka
          Granthalayam continues to uphold its founding principle: that
          democratic access to books, ideas, and shared dialogue is essential
          for an informed and compassionate community.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Footer Note -->
      <footer
        class="border-t border-zinc-300 pt-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-4 font-mono text-xs text-zinc-600"
      >
        <span>Pazhassi Raja Smaraka Granthalayam &bull; Mananthavady</span>
        <a
          href="/"
          class="font-bold text-[#161616] hover:text-[#D9381E] underline underline-offset-4"
        >
          &larr; Back to Festival Portal
        </a>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
